{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Work on the Spring XD 1.1.0.RELEASE code base with its existing Gradle-based build; no application code changes are required, only benchmarking, documentation, and build/publishing work.",
    "Use the RabbitMQ PerfTest load-generation tool to drive RabbitMQ throughput/latency benchmarks in a topology representative of an XD cluster (single node and clustered configurations).",
    "Use Kafka's built-in performance utilities (kafka-producer-perf-test.sh and kafka-consumer-perf-test.sh) as required by U5, with no custom benchmark tooling development.",
    "Reproduce the LinkedIn reference topology for U5: 3 Kafka brokers on separate EC2 instances, a 3-node ZooKeeper ensemble, replication factor 3, and 6 producer instances, targeting the published ~2M writes/sec baseline.",
    "Publish RPMs to repo.spring.io (libs-release-local) using the existing Gradle Artifactory publishing configuration extended with the spring.io repository target and credentials.",
    "Deliver module descriptions in two forms: concise high-level javadoc at the module definition level (U2) and expanded user-facing descriptions in the reference documentation/wiki (U4).",
    "Deliver the message header change documentation (U6) as a new section in the existing GitHub wiki Deployment troubleshooting page."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are effort (workdays), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "The Spring XD 1.1.0 source tree, build environment, and commit/wiki access are available from day one.",
    "An AWS account with permissions and credentials to create EC2 instances is available; EC2 monetary cost is out of scope.",
    "Spring XD 1.1.0 ships roughly 50 modules (sources, sinks, processors, jobs) that each need a brief high-level description; U4 descriptions are short extensions of the U2 javadoc content.",
    "The Gradle build already produces RPM artifacts; only publishing to repo.spring.io and verification of the published bits are needed for U3.",
    "Kafka version is the one bundled/validated with Spring XD 1.1 (0.8.x line); RabbitMQ version is the version supported by XD 1.1 (3.3.x line).",
    "Benchmark runs include warm-up and repeat executions; wall-clock run time overlaps with light monitoring effort and is charged at monitoring effort, not full hands-on effort.",
    "Existing 1.0 batch-jobs and the documented message header deltas between 1.0 and 1.1 are available as input for U6."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Planning and environment preparation",
      "activity_description": "Review all user stories, confirm scope per story, set up local build of Spring XD 1.1.0, and prepare workstation/tooling (Gradle build, benchmark clients, wiki access).",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "RabbitMQ benchmark environment setup (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Provision and configure RabbitMQ nodes and the PerfTest client environment, including clustered configuration representative of an XD deployment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "RabbitMQ benchmark execution (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Run throughput and latency benchmark scenarios (varying producers, consumers, message sizes, durability) using PerfTest.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "RabbitMQ results analysis and reference report (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Consolidate benchmark results into a reference report usable for sizing an XD cluster and publish it to the wiki.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "High-level module descriptions in javadoc (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Write concise high-level descriptions for each module (~50 modules) in the module definition javadoc and verify generated output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "User-facing module descriptions (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Expand the module javadoc content into user-facing descriptions of purpose and capabilities in the reference documentation/wiki.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "RPM publishing configuration to repo.spring.io (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Extend the Gradle/Artifactory publishing configuration to publish Spring XD RPMs to repo.spring.io libs-release-local, including credentials handling and staging.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Verification of published RPM artifacts (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Publish the 1.1.0.RELEASE RPMs, then download them from repo.spring.io and verify installability and integrity.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "EC2 infrastructure research for Kafka perf tests (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Research and document the EC2 instance types, counts, storage, and network placement needed to reproduce the LinkedIn 'three cheap machines' benchmark topology.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Kafka configuration identification (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Identify and document broker, topic, replication, and OS/JVM tuning configurations required for the performance test setup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Provisioning of Kafka/ZooKeeper cluster on EC2 (U5/U7/U8)",
      "activity_description": "Create EC2 instances, install and configure a 3-node ZooKeeper ensemble and 3 Kafka brokers per the identified configuration, and smoke-test the cluster.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Kafka producer/consumer performance test execution (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Run the built-in producer and consumer perf utilities across the benchmark matrix (message sizes, batch sizes, producer counts, replication, async/sync), including warm-up and repeat runs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Kafka results analysis vs LinkedIn baseline (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Analyze collected metrics, compare against the LinkedIn engineering baseline (~2M writes/sec), explain deviations, and write the benchmark report as the foundation for XD use-cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Message header changes troubleshooting documentation (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Document the 1.0-to-1.1 message header changes, serialization error symptoms, and remediation steps in the wiki Deployment troubleshooting section.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 23.0
  }
}
```

